FINAL CONCLUSION:

Feature engineering is important in time-series forecasting because previous observations can provide useful information about future values. Lag features capture past temperatures, while rolling averages smooth the data.

Random Forest Regression can use these features to predict future temperatures. MAE, RMSE, MAPE, and SMAPE can then be used to evaluate the accuracy of the predictions. Among these metrics, RMSE is especially sensitive to large prediction errors.
